        "paragraphs": [
            "Mistral develops, or makes available, open-weight and commercial large language models. The developer says these models are for broad reasoning, coding, tool use, and agentic tasks, as well as document understanding, speech transcription, and speech generation. The family includes generalist models such as Mistral Large 3, Mistral Medium 3.5, and Mistral Small 4, alongside specialist lines for OCR, audio, code, embeddings, and moderation and safety. Sizes range from Ministral 3 3B to Mistral Medium 3.5, a 128B dense model, and Mistral Small 4, which has 119B total parameters with 6B active parameters per token.",
            "Mistral offers these models through its platform and API, with regional endpoints that let customers choose whether inference runs in Europe or the US, and a Priority Tier in public preview. Mistral says Mistral Medium 3.5 is its first flagship merged model, released as open weights under a modified MIT license, and that Mistral Small 4 is released under the Apache 2.0 license. The developer also says its platform will support third-party open models, starting with Z.ai's GLM-5.2, running on the same infrastructure, regional controls, and service commitments as Mistral models."
        ],
